# WhatsApp Notifier - Copilot Instructions

## Project Overview

This is a Go service for sending WhatsApp notifications. It currently provides
the API foundation from `go-api-template`; the WhatsApp provider has not been
selected or integrated yet.

**Module**: `whatsapp-notifier`

## Project Structure

```text
cmd/main.go       Application entry point
app/              Dependency wiring and route registration
config/           Configuration loading and validation
http/             HTTP handlers and middleware
http_server/      HTTP server implementation
model/            API models
o11/              OpenTelemetry setup
repository/       Persistence layer
services/         Business services
```

## Development Guidelines

- Follow idiomatic Go naming, error handling, and package organization.
- Format changes with `gofmt` and validate them with `go vet ./...` and
  `go test ./...`.
- Keep credentials and API tokens out of source control.
- Keep provider-specific WhatsApp behavior behind a small interface.
- Keep HTTP handlers focused on validation and response mapping; place
  notification logic in services.
- Add tests for new handlers, services, and configuration validation.

## Current Capabilities

- HTTP server with graceful shutdown
- JWT authentication
- Health, version, metrics, and Swagger endpoints
- Structured logging and OpenTelemetry support

## Next Steps

- Select Meta WhatsApp Cloud API or a WhatsApp Web client.
- Add provider configuration and credentials.
- Implement an authenticated notification endpoint.
- Handle delivery status, persistence, and retry behavior.
